WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.709
Lab 2 runs the same gate in
an Azure test subscription,

2
00:00:03.709 --> 00:00:06.037
in a test tenant, never production.

3
00:00:06.037 --> 00:00:09.936
You need a reader identity, a person
who can create policy and role

4
00:00:09.936 --> 00:00:13.762
assignments there, and a second
person to approve the plan's hash.

5
00:00:13.762 --> 00:00:17.159
The subscription may have no
Service Health events at all,

6
00:00:17.159 --> 00:00:18.574
and that's a valid result.

7
00:00:18.574 --> 00:00:22.497
Grant the reader Reader and Service
Health Security Reader, sign in,

8
00:00:22.497 --> 00:00:27.118
and cross-check Learn's own query against
the kit's collection; the counts should

9
00:00:27.118 --> 00:00:31.600
agree, once the merge of one event across
subscriptions is taken into account.

10
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.607
Then plan the alert policy
at the test subscription,

11
00:00:34.607 --> 00:00:39.012
apply it with the approved hash, and
check the remediation and the alert rule.

12
00:00:39.012 --> 00:00:42.699
To back it out, plan the rollback,
have it approved, apply it,

13
00:00:42.699 --> 00:00:47.013
delete what the remediation created,
and remove the reader's roles.

14
00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:50.901
Deleting the assignment doesn't
delete what its remediation made.

15
00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:56.140
The authors haven't run Lab 2; the
workbook's Chapter 1 has the exact commands.
